  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Building resilience in quechua communities in Northern Potos&#xED;</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Bolivia is being severely affected by climate change. Every year, droughts, floods, fires, landslides and other natural disasters are more prolonged and more severe, affecting peoples&apos; lives and livelihoods. The project will be implemented in one of the poorest areas of Bolivia; Northern Potos&#xED; and will benefit indigenous Quechua communities. The project aims at strengthening local communities&apos; capacities and resilience strategies amid climate change. The project will also support capacity building for increasing agroecological production as well as the implementation of infrastructure for water.</narrative>
  </description>
